{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376812-a-competition-exalted-in-the-far-future","id":1376812,"title":"A competition (Exalted in the far-future)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-27T09:08:28-07:00","id":1376812,"title":"A competition (Exalted in the far-future)","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">There was an air of excitement in the arena. The contest was here once again, once every ten years. The people crowded around on the concrete and plastic stands, eagerly watching the two contestants down below in the circular arena lit by the lights. Countless billions more were watching this from their own holographic channels with their eyes, or cameras, or other analogues all across the planet and beyond, but there was a special prestige in being able to witness the events themselves.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">On one side, was a single female, caught in the cusp between womanhood and girlhood. Her face was slim, cheekbones high, hair framing a beautiful face. Her body showed the slight curves of an adult, and her body posture was one of relaxation and slight boredom. Her clothing was nondescript, a simple sari draped over her frame, a reminiescent of the Great Upheavel.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Her opponent was something else. A frame the size of a house, built on multiple legs to spread its weight around and keep its balance. A biomechanical being (not monstrosity, that would be too rude). A leathery skin, with dozens upon dozens of eyes studded over the interior, crystalline lenses staring unblinking into its surroundings. Things moved underneath its skin. Genesis macro-assemblers and containment chambers shifted and moved, its frame powered by a miniature fusion plant.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A tinkle, and the crowd cheered, the stage darkening to show the three judges standing before a table. The lead judge stood forward, and made a speech, telling all how welcome they were.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;And for the 85th iteration of the biotechnological summit convocation.... we have Trevor versus Pacifica! May both of you please come forward and present your items?&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The lumbering giant stood forward first, and placed a delicate creature in the front of the judges. Its fur was silver, and it... flew about the air, displaying a movement and beauty of pure coordination and spatial reckoning. Its eyes glistened in the stage lights, and it let out a sonorous howl, both song and animal cry.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The judges clapped. &quot;A biological anti-gravity function? How amazing! Would you tell us about how you accomplished it.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The machine complied, and launched into a great half-hour speech, speaking of the construction of the creature. The hyperspecialized sugars and organ systems created to power the anti-gravity system. The new brain structure needed to control this new form of movement. The thousands of failures. The years of practice needed to perfect its construction. Every muscle, every single hair, every single nerve, all the while gesticulating with its limbs and its eyes flashing, its contralto voice with barely any human inflection enunciating each word clearly.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The judges then turned to the girl. &quot;Pass.&quot; was all she said. And then she produced a single flower, growing from a pot, its petals glistening in the artifical light. At this, there was a great uproar from the crowd. A combination of outrage, awe.... and despair. The judges simply nodded, and grasped both of them, the creature enthusiastically snuggling into the crook of a single arm, the pot in the hands of another.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Three days later, they were standing in the same location. And the winner was once again, announced.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;Pacifica wins!&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">There was silence at this, barely any sound was made. The crowd was not surprised at this. The only sound came from the newcomers, who were not quite used to this. Why would anyone be surprised? After all, she had won the previous 85 competitions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The machine turned around. This was usually the moment when both participants would graciously congragulate one another. In a fairy tale or a bedtime story, this would occur.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This, however, is reality.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The machine let out a howl that was a combination of machine, beast, and human. Its black leathery skin shook, even as a clicking sound erupted from within as biomechanical assemblers went into a frenzy as its own emotional systems went into haywire. Its legs pounded the concrete pavement, sending cracks spiralling through it. Its eyes wept nanite-filled liquids, even as its body bowed down in a simulation of a predator, exposing the pods where 17 of the world's greatest scientists had wired their brains together into a single functional organism.<br /> <br /> Cyberware and mechanical implants sparked, even as a voice, now distraught and all too human, screamed:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;Why? Thousands of weeks and work, enough resources to buy the continent over again and again. All wasted! What did you do, spend fifteen minutes creating that damned potted plant? Why?&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">It pause for breathe. And asked the question on every single human's mind and their descendent subspecies, howling into the heavens to long-dead gods.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">&quot;WHY CAN'T WE BEAT YOU?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Pacifica bowed forward, in complete respect, not a single muscle moving in her face. The only thing showing was the golden glow from her skin and the circle on her forehead. Turning around, she simply walked out of the arena. What was there to say? They already knew the answer.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A/n: Apologies if there was confusion. I made this in response to a question I had. What if solars were to be present within a post-human civilisation? The kind of civilisation that has perfected gene-hacking, where people upload themselves into computers or clouds of nanites, where people connect themselves into vast networks, sublimating themselves into the hive mind. What then, of the Exalted?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">They would be the ultimate throwback (I know that's not the right word). They would remind the world that, for all the talk of abandoning bodies and upgrading minds the advances in humans... there would still be that one thing that tells them that they're wrong. That the future isn't in the hands of the ones with the most processing power, or the best gene mods. Its whoever starts glowing and has a battle aura.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Apologies if I'm not quite getting my point across. I'm staying up way too late to make this.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 03-28-2020, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T11:02:53-07:00","id":1376823,"title":"","content":"I enjoyed the story, but I don't get how the winner wins. Does their winning entry have countless hidden miraculous properties which are left to the imagination of the reader?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T11:19:43-07:00","id":1376828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376812-a-competition-exalted-in-the-far-future?p=1376823#post1376823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoyed the story, but I don't get how the winner wins. Does their winning entry have countless hidden miraculous properties which are left to the imagination of the reader?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry about this. <br /> <br /> I'm not very.... Good at the whole 'hyper advanced biology' thing. Call it the limit of the writer. Just take my word for it thst in a future where humans genetically engineer one another and upload themselves into foglets that they can basically scan the entirety of a living creature in a few days time, along with the notes both participants are given.<br /> <br /> So anyway, what's your opinion on exalted in a far future setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T11:55:41-07:00","id":1376835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376812-a-competition-exalted-in-the-far-future?p=1376828#post1376828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry about this.<br /> <br /> I'm not very.... Good at the whole 'hyper advanced biology' thing. Call it the limit of the writer. Just take my word for it thst in a future where humans genetically engineer one another and upload themselves into foglets that they can basically scan the entirety of a living creature in a few days time, along with the notes both participants are given.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, the story was fun and got its point across.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376812-a-competition-exalted-in-the-far-future?p=1376828#post1376828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So anyway, what's your opinion on exalted in a far future setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a far future setting, I would expect Infernals to take a prominent place in the setting. First because of their trans-humanist themes, and second because the advance of technology mixed with the death of taboos and traditions would put the Yozis in a decent spot to attempt an escape, or at least exert more influence in the world.<br /> <br /> Posthumanism signals the end of DB hegemony over civilization. In a world where people abandon their human bodies, DBs devolve into an inbred cult of bioconservatives barely holding their grounds against the amalgam golems and computing clouds that rule the world.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are in a constant war against extremists who invite the Wyld into creation on purpose to help modify their own bodies.<br /> <br /> Lunars have reshaped their Castes once again. Faced with foes who have lost their humanity and can no longer have their shapes stolen, Luna's chosen have repurposed themselves as go-betweens who navigate between the worlds of humans and posthumans with ease.<br /> <br /> Abyssals have embraced Posthumanism as a roundabout way of ending life on Creation. They push people and societies to fully transform themselves into machines, snatching the souls of those who transform themselves and taking control of the resulting machines as they would the undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 03-27-2020, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T15:23:53-07:00","id":1376863,"title":"","content":"I tend to think they'd remain awesome, human hearted heroes, in a setting where they probably weren't the biggest things about, but what was bigger than them was generally decidedly pretty posthuman, in ways both good and bad.<br /> <br /> The other alternative is you kind of cramp your posthumanism in its scale and power to not upstage the Exalted (which is pretty lame if you're *into* transhumanist sci fi), or you take Exalted far away from their genre inspirations in order to make them some vaguely Exalted shaped thing on a vastly exaggerated scale. Neither I'm too into.<br /> <br /> YMMV. But main point is, I probably wouldn't do that with the Exalted (they fit well in their own universe, or side tripping over to another fantasy one). So my option is kind of a &quot;If you put a gun to my head...&quot; sort of a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T00:26:13-07:00","id":1376926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376812-a-competition-exalted-in-the-far-future?p=1376835#post1376835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Posthumanism signals the end of DB hegemony over civilization. In a world where people abandon their human bodies, DBs devolve into an inbred cult of bioconservatives barely holding their grounds against the amalgam golems and computing clouds that rule the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amalgam golems? You mean the spell? Or people boosted by cyberware and genetic engineering?<br /> <br /> I'm, well, thinking. Dragonblooded are humans. Superhumanly boosted elementally-charged superhumans. But humans nonetheless. Which means that there's potential there.<br /> <br /> Think not 'bioconservative' dragonblooded, but dragonblooded who have decided to dedicate themselves to improving their base stats. They use enhancements and hardware and software that are artifacts, composed out of jade. Genetic treatments and engineering that work only for one family, similar to many dragonblooded charms. Cybernetic implants that would not work unless they had a large and steady supply of electricity given to them... or enhanced by a dragonblooded lore charm that gives their hardware infinite energy to spend. Those human hybrids that have several minds communing together for greater effect? Dragonblooded do it better, especially amongst their bloodline families, their teamwork powers working together for greater effect. <br /> <br /> Now, we know that there's a limit for everything. Dreams of the first age (we all have complaints about it, yes I know) tells us that moving away too far from the human form means that you can't develop new charms. But I think that there's lots and lots of potential for a shadowrun or any kind of post and trans-human conflict. <br /> <br /> There's nothing saying that Dragonblooded can't take technology and use it as well. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T00:40:39-07:00","id":1376932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376812-a-competition-exalted-in-the-far-future?p=1376863#post1376863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to think they'd remain awesome, human hearted heroes, in a setting where they probably weren't the biggest things about, but what was bigger than them was generally decidedly pretty posthuman, in ways both good and bad.<br /> <br /> The other alternative is you kind of cramp your posthumanism in its scale and power to not upstage the Exalted (which is pretty lame if you're *into* transhumanist sci fi), or you take Exalted far away from their genre inspirations in order to make them some vaguely Exalted shaped thing on a vastly exaggerated scale. Neither I'm too into.<br /> <br /> YMMV. But main point is, I probably wouldn't do that with the Exalted (they fit well in their own universe, or side tripping over to another fantasy one). So my option is kind of a &quot;If you put a gun to my head...&quot; sort of a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... got good inspirations for the 'transhuman sci-fi' thing? Or good recommendations? There's not a lot of work this time around, so I got some spare time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T00:44:20-07:00","id":1376934,"title":"","content":"Could you do something about the formatting tags? They\u2019re a little distracting, I\u2019m having trouble reading the OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T00:46:54-07:00","id":1376936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376812-a-competition-exalted-in-the-far-future?p=1376934#post1376934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you do something about the formatting tags? They\u2019re a little distracting, I\u2019m having trouble reading the OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. First made on reddit, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T04:09:31-07:00","id":1376947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376812-a-competition-exalted-in-the-far-future?p=1376932#post1376932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... got good inspirations for the 'transhuman sci-fi' thing? Or good recommendations? There's not a lot of work this time around, so I got some spare time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like a lot of the standard cited stuff like Banks' Culture novels and Greg Egan's stuff. There's probably much more stuff that really digs deeply into posthumanity, but I have to admit I don't read enough sci-fi any more these days, certainly not really that far future post-human subgenre that split off from space opera in the 1980s-1990s (I kind of cashed out of reading those sort of novels probably in the mid-late 2000s).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T05:35:43-07:00","id":1376948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376812-a-competition-exalted-in-the-far-future?p=1376926#post1376926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amalgam golems? You mean the spell? Or people boosted by cyberware and genetic engineering?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant hive mind machines like the guy in your story made from 17 people.<br /> <br /> I like your take on DBs using their elemental affinities to craft unique body modifications, definitely a kinder fate for them than my own take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T06:16:51-07:00","id":1376954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1376812-a-competition-exalted-in-the-far-future?p=1376948#post1376948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant hive mind machines like the guy in your story made from 17 people.<br /> <br /> I like your take on DBs using their elemental affinities to craft unique body modifications, definitely a kinder fate for them than my own take.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm... half agreeing, and half disagreeing.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I agree with the idea that they'll have some resistance. But here's the thing. Yeah, sure, starting dragonblooded have some trouble... but the issue with dragonblooded is: <br /> <br /> 1. They're the weakest of the exalts. <br /> 2. They've got teamwork<br /> 3. Dragonblooded tend to form families. <br /> 4. There are limits. Sooner or later, they'll get beaten.... like that Culture novel. But its not without a fight. They'll adapt, create, and get new charms. <br /> <br /> In the culture novel, there was a civilisation that fought The Culture and lost. They were immortal aliens with incredible physical and mental stats, and their ships were piloted by several of them linking together to fight the incredibly advanced Culture. They lost... but they put up a hell of a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}